WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.736
-Ron Burgundy, everybody!
Ron Burgundy!

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.104
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.640
Wow. That was some funny --
That was some funny stuff.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.975
-Well, it must have gone well.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.177
You invited me back over
to the couch.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.346
-That's some funny stuff
over there.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.882
-Sorry. I got a little hot
under the collar about Mendes.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:19.052
-Yeah, no problem. I didn't
even know that you did standup.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.520
-Oh, yes.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.057
It's been a lifelong passion
of mine for about a week now.

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:28.695
And I just love it.
It's all about the Benjamins.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.496
You know what I mean, Jimmy?
-No.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:31.865
-The Benjamins.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.065
I don't know what you mean.

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:34.800
-You know.
-No, I don't.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.303
Uh, do you do it on tour?

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:40.640
-Well, I'm on tour right now.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.676
In fact, tomorrow night
I'm opening for Jerry Seinfeld

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.244
at Madison Square Garden.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:48.147
[ Laughter ]
-Really?

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:50.416
-Tickets available
on Ticketmaster.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:51.751
-Is that right?

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.119
-It's Jerry Seinfeld,
Ron Burgundy,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.588
and the Rolling Stones.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.892
With special guest star
KC and The Sunshine Band.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.493
The Roots
are going to be playing.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.461
-Hey. Congratulations.
That's great.

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:05.198
-And jazz vocalist
Bobby McFerrin.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.966
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:10.503
-What a bill.
What an absolute bill.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:13.072
Oh, I don't want
to miss that one.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.807
-It was tough to land Bobby.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.375
-You got him there, though.
-We got him.

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:17.677
-You got him, man.
You got him.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.445
-I said, "I'm not doing it
without McFerrin."

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:20.980
-Yeah, you said that?

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.682
-And they said, "Well, wait
by the phone." But we got him.

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:26.218
But tickets are still available
for tomorrow night.

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:27.387
Madison Square Garden.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.621
-Madison Square Garden.
A lot of people.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.189
-Huge. It's huge.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.925
-Dude, I have to be honest,
I miss you doing the news.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:35.328
-Oh. Well, thank you.
-Do you miss doing the news?

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.930
-Of course I do. Of course I do.
-You do. Yeah.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.468
-Anyone who has walked away
from the news game,

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:44.070
any former journalist who says
they don't miss it is lying.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.340
And I'm talking to you,
Tom Brokaw.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.875
Get your [bleep] together
and get back on the air.

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:51.878
-All right. Hold on now, Ron.
Hold on now, Ron.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.080
Now just...

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.582
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.582 --> 00:02:00.153
Let's get back on board here.
Let's talk about this podcast.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.387
"The Run Burgundy Podcast."

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.956
Season two launched today.
iHeartRadio.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.991
iHeart.com. The app.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:07.893
Where do you podcast from?

00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:09.962
-A room.

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:12.131
A room with a microphone
and chairs.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.400
-Yeah. That's the setup there?
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.269
It's myself,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.205
my assistant and producer,
Carolina,

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.740
and a bottle of Scotch.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.510
We just keep it loosey goosey.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.611
-Wow.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:25.912
-Yeah.
-Interesting.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.847
-It's all about the Benjamins.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:30.282
Well, you say that because every
episode starts with a sponsor

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:32.785
on all of your episodes
of the podcast.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.687
Is there any sponsors
you turn down?

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.689
-Oh, of course. All the time.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.857
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.091
Jimmy, I'm not --

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:40.993
You know, I don't have to
listen to the man. No.

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.329
No, no. So I turn things down
all the time.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.932
-Who have you turned down?
-Unless they offer me cash.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.834
-And then --
-It's all about the Benjamins.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:51.204
-I'll say it, it's all about --
or the Grover Clevelands.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.838
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:54.440
He's the face
of the $1,000 bill.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.209
-Oh, is he really?
-I carry thousands.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.977
I usually walk around
with thousands.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.979
-You carry a wad of
a thousand-dollar bills?

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.847
-A wad of thousand-dollar bills
that people are handing me back

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:03.249
'cause they're like,
"I can't cash this."

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:08.387
-Yeah. It creates more problems
than it solves.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.489
-So you hand someone
a thousand-dollar bill,

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.292
and they hand it back to you?

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:16.028
-So, I'll get, like, a pint
of milk at the grocery store.

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:17.596
-You go out and get a pint?
-Yeah.

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:18.731
What is that? About --
What does that run you?

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.534
About $1.20? $1.20.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:25.637
I'll slap down
a Grover Cleveland.

00:03:25.637 --> 00:03:27.373
And they'll go, "Is that fake?"

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:30.076
A crisp Grover Cleveland.
-Crisp Grover Cleveland.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:32.979
You don't even fold them.
-I don't even fold them.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.280
-You make your pockets longer

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.382
so that you don't
have to fold your money.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.618
-Right. Keep it...
-Flat.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.219
-...in a sleeve,
a plastic sleeve.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:43.856
And I pop it out, snap it.
Grover Cleveland.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.124
-Yeah.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:46.926
-And they're like,
"First of all, is this real?"

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.428
And they're like,
"We can't cash this."

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.828
-"There's nothing we can do."
Yeah.

00:03:49.828 --> 00:03:51.363
-I'm like,
"Can I take it, though?

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:52.831
'Cause all I have
are thousands."

00:03:52.831 --> 00:03:54.366
-Yeah. And do they let you
have the milk?

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:55.535
-Usually.
-Yeah.

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.203
I've listened to some
of your interviews,

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.138
and they're fantastic.
I'm just going to ask you,

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.341
has there ever been an interview
that's gone wrong?

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:05.844
-There has. Two words.
Kylie Minogue.

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:07.213
-Ooh, that's unfortunate.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.081
-Yeah. I mean, you've been
in that situation before.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:11.884
Like, you know, you never
want to meet your heroes.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:15.421
And, boy, Kylie and I,

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:18.891
from the moment
she came into the studio,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:22.695
we just looked at each other,
and it was on.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:25.130
-That's terrible.
I mean, Kylie Minogue?

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:28.233
-And she just bit me
right in the ass.

00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:29.802
-I don't even know
what that means.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.437
-And then when she was done,

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.338
she bit me
in the [bleep] and balls.

00:04:33.338 --> 00:04:36.542
So it was -- It was --

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.876
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:39.278
I mean, that thing...

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:40.946
-What are you talking --
What are you talking about?

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:43.015
-We didn't even get a word out!
-What are you talking about?

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:44.517
-It was just --
-What the hell are you --

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.852
What the hell
are you talking about?

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:47.853
-We just --
-What do you even want?

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:50.122
-We just smelled
each other's pheromones!

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:51.490
It turned into a knife fight!

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.459
-What? With Kylie Minogue?

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:56.361
-With Kylie Minogue.
The great Kylie Minogue.

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:58.230
-The great Kylie Minogue.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.499
-Great, beautiful
Kylie Minogue.

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.501
She got into a knife fight?
-Here's the irony.

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:06.071
We ended up in the emergency
room covered in cuts.

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:09.207
I mean, I looked like The Mummy.
I had bandages all over me.

00:05:09.207 --> 00:05:10.776
And we're lying next to
each other, and we're like,

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:12.445
"What the hell happened?"

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.847
"I think you're great."

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:16.182
And she's like,
"I like you, too."

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.817
And we're good friends now.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:20.753
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.755
-I couldn't take you
as a Kylie Minogue fan,

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.223
to be really honest.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.858
-Oh. I was so nervous
around her.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.026
-Really?

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:28.961
-I think I wanted
to tear her down.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:32.798
-Name one of her songs.
-I'll name you 50.

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:34.500
-I don't have time for that.
-Oh, okay.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.136
-Why don't you give me one --
Give me three songs.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.071
-Three songs.
-By Kylie Minogue.

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:40.272
One or three, yep.

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:43.809
Give me any Kylie Minogue song
that you love.

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:46.946
-Okay.
"Take Me to the River."

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:50.215
Um, "Hot Air Balloon for Two."

00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:51.817
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:53.352
-And then "Sydney Nights."

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:55.921
-Okay. Yeah.
She's from Australia.
She's Australian, yes.

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:59.292
We only have time for a couple
rapid-fire questions.

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:00.926
-Oh, sure, sure, sure.
-Is that okay?

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:03.629
-Yeah. I love this.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.432
-Favorite food.
-Pop-Tarts.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.935
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:18.010
-Favorite animal?
-The meerkat.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.512
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:22.215
-Favorite article of clothing?
-Brass knuckles.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.449
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.051
-Favorite mode
of transportation?

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.319
-Pass.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:29.088
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.457
-Favorite kitchen accessory?
-Wait. What was that?

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:34.459
-Favorite kitchen accessory?
-Oh, belt sander.

00:06:34.459 --> 00:06:35.861
-[ Laughs ] Ron Burgundy.

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:37.296
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:40.599
And thank you for everything
you've done for this world.

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:42.334
-Thank you.
-Ron Burgundy, everyone.

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:46.105
Season two of "The Ron Burgundy
Podcast" launched today.

